Project: meetingmind-v2, branch rag-only. A meeting-transcript QA system with
hybrid vector retrieval and a three-node LangGraph RAG agent. The knowledge
graph and the vector/graph router were measured, neither store dominated, and
both were removed on this branch. They remain on `main` as a recorded
experiment. Do not reintroduce them.

ENVIRONMENT
- Python 3.14 in .venv at the repo root. Windows, Git Bash.
- Groq (openai/gpt-oss-20b by default, override with GROQ_MODEL). Multiple keys
  via GROQ_API_KEYS. The llama-3.1-8b-instant and llama-3.3-70b-versatile
  models were removed from the Groq free tier; do not reintroduce them.

HARD RULES
- NO async, NO threading, NO asyncio.gather, NO concurrent.futures.
  Every LLM call is sequential. Parallel calls exceed the rate limit instantly.
- Every LLM call goes through engine.llm.complete. Never instantiate an API
  client anywhere else. Never bypass the disk cache.
- Pin exact versions for anything added to requirements-v2.txt.
- No try/except that swallows an exception silently. Log it or re-raise.
- Never commit .env or anything containing an API key.

ARCHITECTURE
- engine/ holds all logic. scripts/ holds runnable entry points. app.py is UI only.
- LangGraph nodes are thin wrappers around engine functions. Retrieval logic
  never lives inside agent.py.
- Chroma collections use hnsw:space cosine explicitly. The L2 default degrades
  normalized embeddings.
- Every chunk and every answer carries the turn id it came from.
  Citations depend on it.

LOCKED DECISIONS, do not propose alternatives
ChromaDB file-backed, rank-bm25 fused with RRF, local cross-encoder rerank,
LangGraph, single agent. No Postgres, no pgvector, no Neo4j, no Qdrant, no
vector-DB migration, no knowledge graph, no text classifier, no multi-agent
supervisor.

SCOPE
Do not add features that were not asked for. No config abstraction layers,
no plugin systems, no extra CLIs, no logging frameworks, no type-checking
setup, no CI config, no Dockerfile. If you think something is missing, say so
in your reply instead of building it.

WORKFLOW
Build one stage at a time. After each stage, list the files you touched, give
the verification command, commit, push, then stop and wait.
